From 7e172c9fb74fb62f9a70d999647445932e50891e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dolbaras <dolbaras@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:04:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] scrap: hardware H.264/H.265 decoding with Android
 MediaCodec

The mediacodec feature did not build (new_decoders() did not exist, the
Decoder fields had the wrong type, its match arms duplicated the hwcodec
ones) and, with hwcodec enabled, the software decoder was always chosen
first. Rewrite it:

- pick a hardware decoder with NV12 output from the codec list the
  Android side sends (get_codec_info), skipping .secure ones;
- configure with the real picture size parsed from the SPS of the key
  frame (0x0 makes Amlogic HEVC allocate 4096x2304 buffers), recreate on
  size changes;
- request low latency ("low-latency", "vendor.low-latency.enable");
- render into the Surface of the Flutter texture when the app has set
  one (FFI.setVideoSurface): a render thread shows the newest ready
  frame, the video thread only queues input. No colour conversion and
  no copies, which a Mali-450 needs at 2560x1080 30 fps;
- otherwise (no surface, second decoder) ByteBuffer output converted
  from NV12 with libyuv, honouring stride, slice-height and crop; the
  ndk 0.7 wrapper returns INFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT/BUFFERS_CHANGED as errors;
- wait up to 1 s for the first input buffer and frame (the decoder
  allocates its surface buffers first; the client drops a codec whose
  first frame fails), report a stall as an error;
- log the decoder events to logcat (tag rustdesk-mc), the RustDesk log
  file is often not created on Android.

Decoder: try the media codec before the software decoder; on any error
drop it and continue with the software decoder (the client requests a
key frame after a decode error); frames shown on the texture are passed
on with pixelbuffer = false. Prefer H.264 when the codec choice is Auto
and a hardware H.264 decoder exists: hardware H.265 decoders may hold
the last frame until the next one arrives.
