+//! H.264/H.265 decoding with the Android MediaCodec hardware decoders.
+//!
+//! When the app has handed over the Surface of the Flutter texture the remote
+//! screen is shown on (FFI.setVideoSurface), the decoder renders into it
+//! directly: no colour conversion and no copies, the GPU draws the frame.
+//! A render thread takes the decoded frames and shows them, so the video
+//! thread only queues input and never waits for the decoder.
+//! Otherwise (or for a second decoder) it runs in ByteBuffer mode and the
+//! decoded NV12 frame is converted to RGB with libyuv, like the software path.
+//!
+//! Notes from testing on an Amlogic S905L2 TV box (Android 9, OMX.amlogic.*):
+//! - only NV12 (color-format 21) output is offered, I420 (19) is not;
+//! - configuring 0x0 makes the HEVC decoder allocate 4096x2304 buffers, so
+//!   the real size is taken from the SPS of the key frame;
+//! - the output format always reports the configured size (a bigger stream
+//!   is scaled down); the client draws frames at the remote display size, so
+//!   the decoder is configured with exactly that size;
+//! - "vendor.low-latency.enable" makes the H.264 decoder return every frame at
+//!   once instead of holding the last one;
+//! - frames with several slices make the H.264 decoder stall, so a stall is
+//!   reported as an error and the caller falls back to the software decoder.
